Roundcube Webmail on FenrirOS
=============================

Code: /usr/share/roundcube (config/ is /etc/roundcube, temp/ is
/var/lib/roundcube/temp, logs/ is /var/log/roundcube). PHP runs as _php
(php-fpm). Nothing is configured: Roundcube does not start until
/etc/roundcube/config.inc.php exists. The web installer is not shipped.

1. Database. MariaDB:
     CREATE DATABASE roundcubemail CHARACTER SET utf8mb4 COLLATE utf8mb4_unicode_ci;
     CREATE USER 'roundcube'@'localhost' IDENTIFIED BY '<password>';
     GRANT ALL ON roundcubemail.* TO 'roundcube'@'localhost';
   (PostgreSQL works the same way; SQLite needs only a file writable by
   _php, e.g. sqlite:////var/lib/roundcube/roundcube.db?mode=0640.)
2. cp /etc/roundcube/config.inc.php.sample /etc/roundcube/config.inc.php,
   chown root:_php and chmod 640 it, then set:
     $config['db_dsnw']   = 'mysql://roundcube:<password>@localhost/roundcubemail';
     $config['imap_host'] = 'ssl://mail.example.org:993';
     $config['smtp_host'] = 'tls://mail.example.org:587';
     $config['des_key']   = '<24 random characters>';   # e.g. openssl rand -base64 18
   The sample's des_key is a placeholder known to everyone; replace it.
3. Create the tables:
     su -s /bin/sh _php -c '/usr/share/roundcube/bin/initdb.sh --dir=/usr/share/roundcube/SQL'
4. Plugins: enable them in $config['plugins']; each one's settings go in
   /etc/roundcube/<plugin>.inc.php, starting from
   /usr/share/roundcube/plugins/<plugin>/config.inc.php.dist.
5. Web server: /usr/share/doc/roundcube/nginx-roundcube.conf; enable
   php-fpm and nginx (dinitctl enable php-fpm nginx).
6. Housekeeping (optional): cp /usr/share/doc/roundcube/roundcube.cron
   /etc/cron.d/roundcube and dinitctl enable crond.

After an upgrade: su -s /bin/sh _php -c '/usr/share/roundcube/bin/updatedb.sh
--package=roundcube --dir=/usr/share/roundcube/SQL'.
